;;; Describe's minimal-line row on a program that states an obligation its root discharges —
;;; the M1e2 no-owner inventory's **F1** (2026-11-06, `F1_trivial_line_stated_obligation.ein`
;;; under `plans/m1e2_correctness/inventory_2026-11-06/findings/` until M1f S1f.5.6 moved it
;;; here, beside its control, `minimal-line-stated-obligation-control.ein`).
;;;
;;; The program states `(total-owed likes is-a)`: every Person likes some Food. Root holds
;;; `(likes Ann Soup)`, so it discharges the one instance, Ann's, and owes nothing; with
;;; `:no-hypothesis` H is empty, so R is {∅}, root itself, and the minimal line is {∅}.
;;;
;;; Until S1f.5.6 the row read `1 state — ∅, the trivial line: no obligation is stated`, here
;;; and on the control alike, since it read whether a node the run met owes and not what the
;;; program states: true of the control, false here. The user ruled S-17 and F1 (a) on
;;; 2026-11-07, *"a, drop the clause"*: on both files the row reads `1 state — ∅`, the `∅` row
;;; above it saying why (root is alive and owes nothing), and `--json-summary`'s
;;; `region.minimal.trivial` reads *∅ is in R*, true on both. `ein-cli/tests/region_modes.rs`
;;; holds the pair.
(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed))
(relation is-a  T T
  :why "{?1} is a {?2}")
(relation likes Person Food
  :why "{?1} likes {?2}")
(is-a Ann Person) (is-a Soup Food)
(total-owed likes is-a)
(likes Ann Soup)
(solve :no-hypothesis (is-a likes))
